            <ArticleTitle>Balkanization Makes It Unclear Just What the Doctor Ordered.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>16-24</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Physicians are a disparate lot. At last count, there were more than 300 member organizations of the American Association of Medical Societies. These organizations tread common ground on a host of issues in play in this upcoming election cycle. They also part ways on some important issues, including their stance on the Affordable Care Act.</AbstractText>
